body:
When a class extends a mixin returning an intersection type (e.g., `typeof MixinClass & T`), overridden static methods lose inherited documentation. This happens because `GetBaseTypes` resolves the intersection constructor type to the return type of the first construct signature, which may not contain all static members from the full intersection.

```ts
declare class BaseClass {
    /** some documentation */
    static method(): number;
}

class MixinClass {}
declare function Mix<T extends AnyConstructor>(BaseClass: T): typeof MixinClass & T;

declare class Mixed extends Mix(BaseClass) {
    static method(): number;
}

Mixed.method;
//    ^ No documentation shown
```

### Changes

- **`internal/checker/exports.go`**: Export `GetApparentType` and `GetBaseConstructorTypeOfClass` from the checker, mirroring the internal pattern the checker already uses for static base type resolution during class checking.
- **`internal/ls/hover.go`**: For static members, use the checker's own `GetBaseConstructorTypeOfClass` + `GetApparentType` to resolve the static base type directly. This correctly preserves the full intersection constructor type from mixins (e.g., `typeof MixinClass & T`), on which `GetPropertyOfType` can find static properties across all constituents. For instance members, the existing `GetBaseTypes` loop is retained.
- **`internal/fourslash/tests/hoverMixinOverrideDocumentation_test.go`**: Test verifying documentation inheritance through mixin overrides.

