The goal of this change is to make injection queries for comment containing documentation markup easier, specifically Doxygen comments.

E.g. consider:

```c
/// \param[in] s1
///     The first string to compare
/// \param[in] s2
///     The second string to compare
int strcmp(const char *s1, const char s2);
```

Without combining the comments, a Doxygen grammar would not be able to see the context needed to parse "The first string to compare" as a description for the `@param` command. But combining just all C++ style comments via the injection query is also not ideal, e.g. consider:

```c
int strcmp(
  const char *s1, ///< [in] s1 The first string to compare
  const char *s2  ///< [in] s2
                  ///<     The second string to compare
)
```

In the postfix style documentation, the `[in]` / `[out]` / `[in,out]` is only expected at the beginning of a comment block. Still, postfix style documentation may span multiple C++ style comments, so just combining all C++ style comments except for postfix style documentation is also loosing relevant context.

Combining related C++ style comments already in the C grammar is an pragmatic solution to this problem.

